From ca949677539e5635beac8e4cbf68aa3856e0951d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:10:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net/ethernet/sdp: add SDP1412 EMAC probe skeleton (patch
 0017)

Add a probe-only skeleton for the Samsung SDP1412 (Nike-L) EMAC
controller and its DT node.  All hardware values come from the
firmware dtb0 (T-NKLDEUC 2743.0 dtb.bin, nikel-2G, sha256 0189cc94,
node /soc/emac) with the locations noted in comments.

DT node emac@120000 in sdp-nikel.dtsi:
  - reg: 5 blocks (0x120000/0x100, 0x120100/0x300, 0x120700/0x100,
    0x120800/0x100, 0x121000/0x100)
  - interrupts: GIC SPI 7
  - clock-names: "emac_clk" (phandle index TBD pending sdp_mac.c import)
  - samsung,pad-ctrl-reg / samsung,phy-sel-reg: firmware values
  - samsung,bus-width = 64, napi-weight = 64, phy-mask = 0
  - status = "disabled"

drivers/net/ethernet/sdp/sdp_mac.c:
  - Maps 5 MMIO regions, gets optional "emac_clk"
  - Returns 0 from probe (skeleton; MAC implementation TBD)
  - clk_get_optional() so it probes in QEMU without a clock provider

Kconfig/Makefile: NET_VENDOR_SDP + SDP_MAC tristate, wired into
drivers/net/ethernet/{Kconfig,Makefile} alphabetically.

No register offsets invented.  Full MAC implementation will follow
after sdp_mac.c (4870 lines, MODULE_LICENSE("GPL")) is imported via
a MODE=show runner run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
